p1_extra = '''    "For international multi-regional marketplaces, programmatic catalog SEO extends into global localization governance via hreflang annotations. When identical or localized product catalogs are published across multiple country storefronts (e.g., US English, UK English, Canadian French, and German), search engines require explicit bidirectional hreflang link tags (`<link rel=\\"alternate\\" hreflang=\\"en-US\\" href=\\"...\\" />`) to prevent cross-border duplicate content penalties. The programmatic URL router dynamically evaluates geo-IP headers and multi-tenant domain configurations, injecting localized canonical tags and hreflang headers directly into HTTP response headers. Furthermore, automated sitemap generators partition XML sitemaps into chunks of 50,000 URLs with gzip compression, continuously updating `<lastmod>` timestamps tied to real-time PIM inventory events to direct Googlebot crawl priority to newly modified products.",'''

