p3_extra = '''    "To push edge rendering performance to its theoretical limit, modern architectures integrate React Server Components (RSC) and Streaming Server-Side Rendering with HTTP Suspense boundaries. Instead of waiting for slow upstream database queries or third-party personalization microservices to finish before returning the first byte, the edge server immediately streams the static HTML document shell, navigation bar, and preloaded hero image to the client in under 20 milliseconds. Non-critical dynamic widgets—such as real-time store availability, personalized cross-sell carousels, and user loyalty points—are wrapped in `<Suspense>` boundaries. As background workers resolve these dynamic microservices, the server streams the resulting HTML chunks down the existing HTTP/2 connection, completely eliminating Time to First Byte (TTFB) delays.",'''

